	(footprint "picoemp:SW_Push_ESwitch_TL3301AJ"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "892aef83-3a9d-4052-aa77-c1c1b0f3a7b0")
		(at 121.1758 121.3083 90)
		(descr "E-Switch TL3301A series 6.0x6.0mm SMT tactile switch, J-lead ('QJ') termination -- per E-Switch's TL3301 Series datasheet (e-switch.com/product-catalog/tl3301-series-smt-tactile-switch), J-Lead Termination PCB Layout drawing. Pad centres at +/-2.785mm X, +/-2.25mm Y (5.57mm x 4.50mm pitch), pad size 2.03x1.40mm, derived from the datasheet's 7.60mm overall pad envelope and 4.50mm row pitch. Deliberately NOT sharing KiCad stock Button_Switch_SMD:SW_Push_1P1T_NO_CK_KSC7xxJ: upstream calls the TL3301A 'same footprint' as the KSC741J, but the two datasheets disagree materially -- 6.0x6.0mm body vs KSC7xxJ's 6.2x6.2mm, and critically a 4.50mm row pitch vs the KSC7xxJ land's 4.00mm, a 12.5% mismatch that would put this part's leads on top of soldermask/copper meant for a different pitch rather than centered on a pad. See Task 8 report for the full comparison.")
		(tags "tactile switch tl3301 e-switch")
